## Context

Child of tracker 1552. Runs `/replicate reproduce` on the Gavard Scotch
reproduction (`~/CNRS/papiers/actif/Gavard Scotch 2026 Climate finance
counterproductive/`, completed by hand, a known answer) plus 2 I4R papers.
Execution environment, ruled by the author on 2026-11-25: no commercial
software is available, so no Stata. R runs in a pinned image (rocker, with
`renv`) that replicator provides; the skill only records the environment in
`manifest.json`. A Stata-only package is transcoded to Python (`pyfixest`
matches `reghdfe`'s small-sample corrections) or R (`fixest`) and reported
as "re-implemented, matched to published figures", not "reproduced from the
authors' package". Gavard Scotch is that case (Stata package, Python port,
known answer). The 2 I4R papers are chosen among packages in R or Python,
so one run executes code as published. For Toulouse the author's plan is
to transcode and rerun before the Games.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] A pinned R environment exists in replicator and is recorded in each
      folder's `manifest.json`; no Stata.
- [ ] `reproduce` run on Gavard Scotch (transcoded, compared with the
      September port) and 2 I4R papers with R or Python packages (run as
      published); for the I4R papers, whether it finds I4R's recorded
      discrepancies.
- [ ] Results in `design/replicate-reproduce-validation-<date>.md`.
